    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0501" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114 EW/12–2944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-29T17:00:00+03:00">December 29,
                            1944—5 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 30—4:30 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5053. I have received a letter from Vyshinski (ReEmbs 4645 December 5, 1 p. m.)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d274-f1"/>
                    stating that Lieutenant General K. D. Golubev and Major
                    General N. V. Slavin have been appointed by
                    the Soviet Government to conduct negotiations with General Deane on questions connected with the plan
                    mutually to repatriate American and Soviet prisoners of war and civilians in
                    accordance with the principles set forth in Molotov’s letter to Kennan of November 25. The pertinent sections of Molotov’s letter were repeated to the
                    Department in Embassy’s telegram 4526 of November 27.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d274-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
